      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "We likely have found the main issue, the user set limits for compressed and uncompressed size were mixed up when evaluating limits, a proper fix is in the works however if you want a temporary solution just max out the compressed limit (download size), do not set it to 0. Only downside is avatars with an uncompressed size greater than 200 MB (the max download size) won't load unless manually shown, which IMO you shouldn't have avatars that take up over 200 MB uncompressed automatically shown unless in small instances",
